    "body": "Expose the \"plus\" variants of `go_in` and `go_out` so that users may\r\ncreate multiple mappings to these actions.\r\n\r\nIt is not currently possible to map more than one key to these actions\r\nwithout implementing their behavior manually, since the only way to map\r\na key to these actions is through the `mappings` table of the `setup()`\r\ncall, which does not support mapping multiple keys to a single action.\r\n\r\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2023-12-29T17:45:28Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for creating this!\r\n\r\nThe current suggestion for multiple mappings in `go_in_plus` and `go_out_plus` is to make custom wrappers. Like ones described in #409.\r\n\r\nBut I think I'll rethink this decision. Either with the approach from this PR or by adding options to `go_in()` and `go_out()`.\r\n\r\nI'll think about it.",
            "created_at": "2023-12-15T16:11:20Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/616#issuecomment-1858124593",
            "id": 1858124593,
