                "user_view_type": "public"
            }
        },
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "After 40086c0a646100c766e8e05cd6e7d75bb1ca37de, `go_in()` now has the `close_on_file` option which can be used in custom mappings. If used `go_in()` directly, it won't support `count`, but I think it is a reasonable compromise.\r\n\r\nAlso decided to not add any option for `go_out()` to emulate `go_out_plus` as it would quite literally be a call to `trim_right()` inside an `if`. I think it is reasonable to leave this kind of functionality to user wrappers.\r\n\r\nAll in all, I am going to close this as there are now reasonably good tools to solve the actual problem.\r\n\r\nThanks again for your time and interest!",
            "created_at": "2023-12-29T17:45:28Z",
